# Every checkout uses LF, so the Prettier check (`pnpm lint`) reports the same result on Linux,
# macOS and Windows: GitHub's Windows runners default to `core.autocrlf=true` and would otherwise
# turn every tracked text file into CRLF before Prettier sees it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures and assets stay byte-for-byte; `text=auto` detects them, this only makes it
# explicit for the formats the engine ships and the tests compare byte counts on.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.wasm binary
*.zip binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.sav binary
